# Copy to .env.local for local development (never commit real keys).
#
# Google Books. PRODUCTION: the app calls /api/google-books (functions/api/google-books.js), which reads the Cloudflare Pages
# SECRET named GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY (Settings -> Variables and Secrets, type: Secret, for Production AND Preview, then redeploy).
# It is NOT a VITE_ variable and never ships in the app. Restrict the key by API (Books API) only, not by HTTP referrer.
#
# LOCAL ONLY, both optional (raise the quota for scripts / the dev server). Never set these as Cloudflare build variables:
#   - `npm run dev` does not run Pages Functions, so ratings in the dev server need the key here;
#   - `npm run prefetch:store` / `npm run check:google` run in Node and also read GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY from the shell environment.
VITE_GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=

# New York Times Books API. LOCAL DEV ONLY: with this set, the app calls the NYT directly.
# In production leave it unset: the app calls /api/nyt (functions/api/nyt.js), which reads the secret NYT_API_KEY
# from Cloudflare Pages -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets (type: Secret), so the key never reaches the browser.
VITE_NYT_API_KEY=
